We've also just discovered that it is possible to make RequireJS work with current build by pointing requireConfig of individual modules to built file, eg: 
```
require.config({
    paths: {
        'transliterate': '../bower_components/transliteration/lib/browser/transliteration',
        'slugify': '../bower_components/transliteration/lib/browser/transliteration',
    }
});
```
and in place of usage requiring individual functions from the module like this:
```
define(['transliterate', 'slugify'], function(transliterate, slugify) {
// ...
});
```
though in my opinion, this is not a way to go because
- in general this way you have to require N modules from one file
- module names specified at definition may lead to name collisions

Works well for me with this configuration

```
require.config({
  paths: {
    transliteration: "lib/transliteration/transliteration.min", // 1.6.2 bower install transliteration@1.6.2
  }
});

...


require(['transliteration', 'slugify'], function(transliteration, slugify) {
  // Use slugify & transliteration here
});
```

