BTW, better keep pairs in Map type - key-value pairs (2-element Arrays):

```
Cyrilic.iso9a.ru = [
// combinations
...
// single chars
  ["а", "a"],
...
  ["я", "ya"]
]
```
- https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Map

And, please, do not uglify sources! Keep each pair in one row - easy to read and convert to other formats (programming languages).

```
Cyrilic.iso9a.ru = {
// combinations
...
// single chars
  "а" => "a",
...
  "я" => "ya"
}
```

dist/transliteration.js - function/API, that transliterates words or sentences
dist/transliteration-data.js - set of character pairs (or formulas), how words should translated.

BTW, check [wiki/Help:Multilingual_support_(Indic)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Multilingual_support_%28Indic%29#Online_transliteration.2Finput), to understand, that other languages transliterates in more complex way.

Function:

```
module.exports = function transliteration(data, req, res) {
    // ... calculations, depending of passed `data`
    return res;
}
```

